    questionText: "When the marbles in a bag are divided evenly between two friends, there is one marble left over. When the same marbles are divided evenly among three friends, there is one marble left over. When divided evenly among five friends, there is again one marble left over.\n(i) What is the least possible number of marbles in the bag?\n(ii) What is another possible number of marbles in the bag?",
    solutionSteps: ["[1 mark] A number leaving remainder 1 on division by 2, 3 and 5 has the form LCM(2, 3, 5) x k + 1. By prime factorization 2 = 2, 3 = 3, 5 = 5, so LCM(2, 3, 5) = 2 x 3 x 5 = 30.", "[1 mark] Least possible number (k = 1): 30 x 1 + 1 = 31 marbles.", "[1 mark] Adding further multiples of 30 gives other possibilities: 30 x 2 + 1 = 61 (also 91, 121, ...)."],
