    questionText: "Kerosene is a combustible hydrocarbon liquid derived from petroleum, used for oil lamps, cleaning, jet fuel, heating and cooking. Two oil tankers contain 825 litres and 675 litres of kerosene oil respectively.\n(i) Find the maximum capacity of a container which can measure the kerosene oil of both tankers an exact number of times.\n(ii) How many times must the container be used for each tanker?",
    solutionSteps: ["[1 mark] The maximum container capacity that exactly measures both quantities = HCF(825, 675).", "[1 mark] By prime factorization: 825 = 3 x 5^2 x 11 and 675 = 3^3 x 5^2.", "[1 mark] HCF = product of lowest powers of common primes = 3 x 5^2 = 75. So the maximum capacity is 75 litres.", "[1 mark] Number of uses = 825/75 = 11 times for the first tanker, and 675/75 = 9 times for the second tanker."],
