    section: "C", marks: 3, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying",
    questionText: "A manufacturer introduces a new line of frying pan. Fixed costs are estimated at Rs 84000 per month, and the components to assemble and test each frying pan run Rs 450 per unit. Consumers are willing to pay at least Rs 690 per unit.\n(i) How many units must be made and sold each month to break even?\n(ii) What is the revenue required to break even?",
    solutionSteps: ["[1 mark] Let u = units made and sold. Cost = 84000 + 450u, Revenue = 690u. Break-even: 690u = 84000 + 450u.", "[1 mark] (i) 690u - 450u = 84000 => 240u = 84000 => u = 350 units per month.", "[1 mark] (ii) Break-even revenue = 690 * 350 = Rs 2,41,500 per month."],
