    questionText: "An alumni association donated Rs 1,00,000 to a college. The college loaned part of it to a science student at 7% interest and the rest to an engineering student at 6% interest. That year the college earned Rs 6350 in interest.\n(i) How much was loaned to the engineering student?\n(ii) How much was loaned to the science student?",
    solutionSteps: ["[1 mark] Let s = amount loaned to science student, e = amount to engineering student. s + e = 1,00,000. Interest: 0.07s + 0.06e = 6350.", "[1 mark] Substitute e = 1,00,000 - s: 0.07s + 0.06(1,00,000 - s) = 6350 => 0.01s + 6000 = 6350 => 0.01s = 350 => s = 35,000.", "[1 mark] (ii) Science student = Rs 35,000; (i) Engineering student e = 1,00,000 - 35,000 = Rs 65,000."],
